# Langfuse Patterns (v4)

## v4 Migration Notes

- Langfuse v4 (March 2026) is a ground-up rewrite with observation-centric data model
- Import from `langfuse` (same package, new API)
- SDK requires Pydantic v2
- See migration guide: https://langfuse.com/docs/observability/sdk/upgrade-path/python-v3-to-v4

## Instrumentation

- Use `@observe()` decorator for auto-capture of inputs, outputs, timings
- Use `@observe(as_type="generation")` for LLM calls (token/cost tracking)
- Use context managers for more reliable control
- Always include `user_id`, `session_id`, `tags`

## Production

- Call `langfuse.flush()` in short-lived processes
- Avoid `ThreadPoolExecutor` for decorated functions
- Tag traces for per-user cost analysis
- Score sample of production traces (not all)
- Gate deploys on regression checks

## Integration

- Use native integrations for LangChain, OpenAI, Anthropic
- Emit OpenTelemetry spans to prevent vendor lock-in
- Use `CallbackHandler` from `langfuse.langchain` (not `langfuse.callback`) for LangChain v3+
